**output-report.hpp encodes complete PlayStation controller output reports for USB/Bluetooth links.**

## Exports

- `ds4_output_usb_size`, `ds4_output_bt_size`, `ds_output_usb_size`, `ds_output_bt_size`: `size_t` report sizes `{32}`, `{78}`, `{63}`, `{78}`.
- `encode_dualshock4_output(const output_request&, connection, span<byte> out) noexcept`: returns `optional<size_t>` byte count or `nullopt` for unsupported/ambiguous requests.
- `encode_dualsense_output(const output_request&, connection, uint8_t& bt_sequence, span<byte> out) noexcept`: returns `optional<size_t>` and increments per-device Bluetooth sequence modulo 16.

## Contracts

`encode_dualshock4_output` and `encode_dualsense_output` require buffers sized for the selected report and reject unrecognized requests; framing follows Linux `hid-playstation.c`. USB uses direct reports; Bluetooth uses DS4 control-byte or DualSense sequence framing plus CRC-32 with output seed.

## Dependencies

`types.hpp` supplies `optional`, `span`, and `byte`; `utility.hpp`, `id.hpp`, and `output.hpp` define encoding primitives, `connection`, and `output_request`.